# Git hooks and shell scripts MUST be checked out with LF endings.
#
# WHY (proven 2026-08-05, not theoretical): this repo sets core.autocrlf=true and had no
# .gitattributes, so a FRESH Windows clone received .githooks/* with CRLF. A CRLF hook has
# a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang and `\r`-terminated patterns in protected-paths, which makes the
# pre-commit gate a silent no-op -- a fresh clone committed a protected path with no
# reviews/DDR-*.md at exit 0, while the same hook enforced correctly in the older working
# copy that happened to still hold LF. The gate reported green where it ran and did nothing
# where it was used.
#
# Do not remove these rules. A gate that cannot be trusted to run is worse than no gate,
# because it buys false confidence.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
